Read CLAUDE.md, docs/DESIGN-CONTRACT.md and this brief's phase before editing.
Hebrew, RTL, logical properties only, every number in <bdi>.
JS on /a/[slug] <= 12 KB gz total, vanilla only. No framework, no animation lib.
Verify every change with Playwright MCP on WebKit iPhone and Chromium Android
before claiming done. Screenshots go in docs/screens/<phase>/.

WHERE THE VERIFICATION CAN ACTUALLY RUN — read before trusting a green report.

WebKit is the whole reason Playwright is in this stack: Israeli traffic is
iPhone-heavy and Chromium-only testing misses Safari bugs. The cloud container
Claude Code runs in has Chromium only, and `npx playwright install webkit`
fails there because the Playwright CDN is blocked by the egress proxy. So:

  - Chromium checks may be run anywhere.
  - EVERY WebKit/Safari claim must come from a machine with WebKit installed,
    which today means the Mac. An agent in the container cannot make one, and
    must say so rather than reporting a Chromium pass as Safari coverage.
  - Context7 is unreachable from the container (proxy returns 403 on CONNECT),
    so version-specific doc lookups also belong to the Mac.
  - chrome-devtools-mcp works in both places; it drives the local Chromium.

Never report an unmeasured number (CLAUDE.md 11.5). "Verified on Chromium,
WebKit not run here" is a complete and acceptable report. "Verified" alone,
when only Chromium ran, is not.
